course: dictionary
lesson: 8827
title: Shia: a branch of Islam
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can name a group of people or a belief. The word «Shia» is a name for one of the two main branches of Islam. Look at the sentence for clues: it mentions Shia Islam, Sunni Muslims, and a capital city, so Shia must be a kind of Islam.
explain: «The Safavid dynasty took power in Persia in 1501 and made Shia Islam the state religion, while their Ottoman neighbours and rivals were Sunni Muslims.» The word «while» shows a contrast: the Safavids followed Shia Islam, and their neighbours followed Sunni Islam. Two branches, two groups, side by side.
explain: Shia Muslims believe that the leader of Muslims after the Prophet Muhammad should have been his cousin and son-in-law Ali, and Ali's descendants. Sunni Muslims followed other leaders, chosen by the community. Both branches share the Qur'an and the main practices of Islam.
explain: Shia can also describe a thing, such as a Shia community. Words can be spelled in different ways: Shi'a and Shiite mean the same thing. When you read about religion, check the dictionary and the sentence, and do not guess.
fact: Shia is one of the two main branches of Islam.
fact: The other main branch is Sunni, and it is the larger one.
fact: A Shia Muslim is a person who belongs to the Shia branch.
fact: Shia Muslims and Sunni Muslims both share the Qur'an and the main practices of Islam.
fact: Most people in Iran and Iraq are Shia, and people of both branches mostly live peacefully side by side.
exercise: «The Safavid dynasty took power in Persia in 1501 and made Shia Islam the state religion.» What is Shia? | A city in Persia | A kind of fruit | *One of the two main branches of Islam | A type of king
exercise: Which branch of Islam is the larger one? | *Sunni | Both are exactly the same size | Shia | Hindu
exercise: «...while their Ottoman neighbours and rivals were Sunni Muslims.» Find and copy the word that names the other branch of Islam. | Ottoman | neighbours | capital | *Sunni
test: A Shia Muslim is a person who... | Is a Christian priest | *Belongs to the Shia branch of Islam | Does not believe in Islam | Lives only in Iran
test: Which of these do Shia and Sunni Muslims share? | *The Qur'an and the main practices of Islam | Different leaders from the start | Only the name Islam | A capital city
exam: Which other spelling of Shia is correct? | Shiny | *Shi'a | Persia | Sunni
